Build CanoKey's virt-card IFD handler without sanitizers.

Upstream defines the u2f-virt-card target ONLY inside `if(ENABLE_TESTS)`, and ENABLE_TESTS
unconditionally adds `--coverage -fsanitize=address -fsanitize=undefined` to every target
(CMakeLists.txt:60-67). pcscd loads this driver with dlopen(), and an ASan runtime that
arrives that late refuses to start:

    ==23==ASan runtime does not come first in initial library list; you should either
    link runtime to your application or manually preload it with LD_PRELOAD.

pcscd then reports "No smart card readers found" and the lane produces nothing.

Upstream's own answer is to LD_PRELOAD libasan/libubsan into pcscd
(.github/workflows/tests.yml:184, test-via-pcsc/run-fido-ci-local.sh:65). That is wrong for
this matrix: it would run the CARD EMULATOR under ASan/UBSan inside a lane that is not an
ASan lane, so a sanitizer abort in CanoKey would be reported as a crash finding against the
module under test (libykcs11.so) -- misattribution of exactly the kind the pool's memory
limits are tuned to avoid. Sanitizer coverage in this repo lives in dedicated *-asan lanes.

The existing VIRTCARD option already gates the virt-card revision-header helper but does
not build the library itself.
This patch exposes the same u2f-virt-card target under VIRTCARD, unchanged apart from
indentation, so `-DVIRTCARD=ON` (without ENABLE_TESTS) yields a clean, uninstrumented
driver. The ENABLE_TESTS path is untouched.

Upstream: https://github.com/canokeys/canokey-core (commit e4a756d61e7a094f84895c7042d4029f7c135820)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -294,6 +294,37 @@
         add_virt_card_git_revision(u2f-virt-card)
     endif()
 endif(ENABLE_TESTS)
 
+# pkcs11-check: build the virt-card IFD handler WITHOUT sanitizers.
+# Upstream defines u2f-virt-card only under ENABLE_TESTS, which unconditionally adds
+# --coverage -fsanitize=address -fsanitize=undefined. pcscd dlopen()s this driver, and an
+# ASan runtime loaded that late aborts with "ASan runtime does not come first in initial
+# library list"; upstream works around that by LD_PRELOADing libasan into pcscd. Doing so
+# here would run the card emulator under ASan inside a NON-asan lane, so any sanitizer
+# abort would surface as a crash finding against the module under test. This repo keeps
+# sanitizer coverage in dedicated *-asan lanes instead, so expose the same target under
+# VIRTCARD, which carries no sanitizer flags.
+if(VIRTCARD AND NOT ENABLE_TESTS)
+pkg_search_module(PCSCLITE libpcsclite)
+if(PCSCLITE_FOUND)
+    add_library(
+        u2f-virt-card
+        SHARED
+        virt-card/usb-dummy.c
+        virt-card/device-sim.c
+        virt-card/ifdhandler.c
+        virt-card/fabrication.c
+        littlefs/bd/lfs_filebd.c
+    )
+    target_include_directories(
+        u2f-virt-card
+        SYSTEM
+        PRIVATE virt-card ${PCSCLITE_INCLUDE_DIRS} littlefs
+    )
+    target_link_libraries(u2f-virt-card ${PCSCLITE_LIBRARIES} canokey-core)
+    add_virt_card_git_revision(u2f-virt-card)
+endif()
+endif()
+
 if(ENABLE_FUZZING)
     add_executable(
         afl-fuzzer
